  data: {
    LLM: 'Game: Baśka (Kashubian Kop). Type: Hidden-partnership point-trick. Rules: 16 cards (A, 10, Q, J). Trumps: Q > J > Hearts (A-10). Total: 104 pts. Goal: 53 pts. 4 tricks total.',
    Player: "Welcome to Baśka! You have just 4 cards. Do you hold a Black Queen? If so, you're an 'Old One'. Hearts are permanent trumps unless you bid 'Gran'. The total is 104 points—can you capture 53 and win?",
    objective: "The 'Old Ones' must capture a majority of the 104 available points in the round (or win all tricks in solo bids).",
    gameplay: "Players must follow suit. Trumps count as their own suit (The 'Trump' suit). If a trump is led, all others MUST play trumps. If an off-suit (e.g., Ace of Spades) is led, players must follow Spades.",
    keyRules: [
      'Point Values: Ace (11), 10 (10), Queen (3), Jack (2). Total = 104 points.',
      'Winning: The declarer/partnership needs 53 points (104 / 2 + 1) to win.',
      "Contra: Opponents can shout 'Kontra' to double the points for the round if they believe they can beat the bid.",
    ],
